        "original_id": "4088a457-2426-5bc3-a48e-65a8340f9645",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edward Dmytryk, Otto Preminger, Alec Coppel\n- Works: Obsession, The Hidden Room, A Man About A Dog\n- Roles: film director, theatre director, screenwriter, novelist\n- Topics: British crime films, American film directors\n\nFacts:\n- Otto Preminger was born on 5 December 1905 and died on 23 April 1986.\n- Edward Dmytryk was born on 4 September 1908 and died on 1 July 1999.\n- Otto Preminger was an American theatre and film director who was originally from Austria-Hungary.\n- Edward Dmytryk was a Canadian-born American film director.\n- Obsession was released in 1949 as a British crime film.\n- Obsession was released in the United States under the title The Hidden Room.\n- Edward Dmytryk directed Obsession.\n- Obsession was based on the book A Man About A Dog by Alec Coppel.\n- Alec Coppel wrote the screenplay for Obsession and also turned the story into a novel.",
